module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.PrincipalFormalLocusTagInjectivity
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.AssociatedPoints
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.Complex
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.CohomologicalDimensionBounds

/-!
# Algebraization at a principal formal locus, under a dimension bound

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, let `f ∈ 𝔞 ⊆ A`, let `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` and let `ℱ` be a
coherent module on `U`. Stacks 0H49 asserts that if `A` is `f`-adically complete and has a
dualizing complex, and if every associated point `x` of `ℱ` outside `V(f)` whose closure meets
`V(f)` outside `V(𝔞)` satisfies `dim(𝒪_{closure{x}, z}) > 2` for every
`z ∈ closure{x} ∩ V(𝔞)`, then the comparison map

`colim_V Γ(V, ℱ) ⟶ lim Γ(U, ℱ / fⁿ ℱ)`

of Stacks 0EG2 is an isomorphism, the colimit being over the opens `V ⊆ U` containing
`U ∩ V(f)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.ComparisonSurjectivity` — the surjectivity half of Stacks 0EG2,
  stated for every Noetherian ring, every pair of ideals `I ⊆ 𝔞` and every coherent module on
  `Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`. It is a hypothesis here, not a theorem: see the implementation notes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.cohomologicalDimension_span_singleton_le_one` — the cohomological
  dimension of a principal ideal of a Noetherian ring is at most one.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.mono_comparisonMap_span_singleton` — **the injectivity half of Stacks
  0H49**, with none of the tag's hypotheses.

Stacks 0H49 itself is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_comparisonMap_span_singleton_of_two_lt_closureLocalDimension`, in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.PrincipalFormalLocusAlgebraization`, which needs no
surjectivity hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

The injectivity half of the tag is unconditional: it is
`Stacks.Algebraization.mono_comparisonMap`, which needs only that `A` is Noetherian and `ℱ`
coherent, and is recorded here specialized to a principal ideal so that the half of 0H49 which
is proved carries the tag.

What is *not* available anywhere in this repository is surjectivity. The module docstring of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.PrincipalFormalLocus` records the inventory: of
Stacks 0EG2 only the injectivity half is proved, and of Stacks 0EIH — the variant criterion
through which the source's own proof of 0H49 passes — likewise only injectivity, the
surjectivity half resting on a sheaf identification `ℱ/fⁿℱ ≅ (M/fⁿM)~|_U` that exists in no
spelling. The source's proof of 0H49 also needs the clause of Stacks 0H48 which recovers the
*middle* comparison from the outer two; only the other clause,
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_comparisonMap_first_of_middle_and_third`, is formalized.

`ComparisonSurjectivity` records surjectivity as a hypothesis: it is the surjectivity
half of Stacks 0EG2 in the generality in which the source states it — over every Noetherian
ring, every pair of ideals and every coherent module, with the source's own dimension bound
`cd(A, I) + 1 < dim(𝒪_{closure{x}, z})`. It is not stated about the module `ℱ` of the
conclusion, and it is not 0H49: 0H49 is the case `I = (f)` with the cruder bound `2 < dim`.

The two bounds are bridged by
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.cohomologicalDimension_span_singleton_le_one`: by Stacks 0DX9 (1) the
cohomological dimension of `(f)` is at most one, so `(cd(A, (f)) + 1).toNat ≤ 2` and the tag's
bound `2 < dim` implies 0EG2's. Both bounds are compared in `WithBot ℕ∞`, the value group
of `Order.krullDim`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H49](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H49)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EG2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EG2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DX9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DX9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u v

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

/-- **The cohomological dimension of a principal ideal is at most one.** A principal ideal of a
Noetherian ring is generated by one element, so Stacks 0DX9 (1) bounds its cohomological
dimension by one. -/
theorem cohomologicalDimension_span_singleton_le_one (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] (f : A) :
    cohomologicalDimension A (Ideal.span {f}) (Ideal.span {f}).fg_of_isNoetherianRing ≤ 1 :=
  cohomologicalDimension_le_card_generators A (Ideal.span {f}) _ (fun _ : Fin 1 => f)
    (by rw [Set.range_const])

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

open Stacks.LocalCohomology

/-- **The surjectivity half of Stacks 0EG2.** For every Noetherian ring `B`, every pair of
ideals `J ⊆ 𝔟` of `B` and every coherent module `G` on `Spec(B) ∖ V(𝔟)` with `B` `J`-adically
complete and carrying a dualizing complex, if every associated point `x` of `G` outside `V(J)`
whose closure meets `V(J)` outside `V(𝔟)` satisfies
`cd(B, J) + 1 < dim(𝒪_{closure{x}, z})` for every `z ∈ closure{x} ∩ V(𝔟)`, then the comparison
map of `Stacks.Algebraization.comparisonMap` is surjective.

This is a hypothesis, not a theorem: nothing in this repository proves the surjectivity half of
Stacks 0EG2. The injectivity half is `Stacks.Algebraization.mono_comparisonMap`, and is
unconditional. -/
def ComparisonSurjectivity : Prop :=
  ∀ (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B] (J b : Ideal B), J ≤ b →
    ∀ (G : (complementZeroLocus B b : Scheme).Modules) [G.IsCoherent],
      IsAdicComplete J B →
      (∃ K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{v} B), Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex K) →
      (∀ x : (complementZeroLocus B b : Scheme),
        x ∈ Stacks.Divisors.associatedPoints G → ¬ J ≤ x.1.asIdeal →
        (∃ y : PrimeSpectrum B,
          x.1.asIdeal ≤ y.asIdeal ∧ J ≤ y.asIdeal ∧ ¬ b ≤ y.asIdeal) →
        ∀ z : PrimeSpectrum B, x.1.asIdeal ≤ z.asIdeal → b ≤ z.asIdeal →
          ((cohomologicalDimension B J J.fg_of_isNoetherianRing + 1).toNat : WithBot ℕ∞) <
            closureLocalDimension B x.1 z) →
      Function.Surjective (ConcreteCategory.hom (comparisonMap B J b G))

/-- **Stacks 0H49, the injectivity half.** For a coherent module `ℱ` on
`U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` over a Noetherian ring `A` and an element `f ∈ A`, the map

`colim_V Γ(V, ℱ) ⟶ lim Γ(U, ℱ / fⁿ ℱ)`

of the tag, the colimit being over the opens `V ⊆ U` containing `U ∩ V(f)`, is a monomorphism.

None of the tag's hypotheses is needed: `A` is not assumed `f`-adically complete, no dualizing
complex is assumed, `f` is not assumed to lie in `𝔞`, and no bound on the local dimensions along
the associated points of `ℱ` is assumed. This is
`Stacks.Algebraization.mono_comparisonMap` at the principal ideal `(f)`. -/
@[stacks 0H49 "injectivity"]
theorem mono_comparisonMap_span_singleton (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (a : Ideal A) (f : A) (F : (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme).Modules) [F.IsCoherent] :
    Mono (comparisonMap A (Ideal.span {f}) a F) :=
  mono_comparisonMap A (Ideal.span {f}) a F

end Stacks.Algebraization

